  "conclusions": [
    "More than2 task workers may overlap another available theorem/elaboration/checking task, but do not subdivide a single expensive decide +kernel reduction.",
    "The existing2 workers can already overlap two expensive declaration tasks; the third task can queue or wait on checked-environment dependencies. Current receipts have no per-proof timings proving an idle-worker bottleneck.",
    "A larger worker count adds stacks and may keep more reduction/checker state live. The measured j2 peak3.83–3.92GB leaves per-job headroom below6GiB, but extra allocation is not measured or reliably linear. Two simultaneous jobs already reached a dated3.99GB global available-commit minimum, so per-job headroom does not establish a global safe j3 margin.",
    "Thread scheduling alone does not select native_decide, skipKernelTC, change theorem bodies or change the intended axiom trust boundary. Every new run still needs exact source/output/raw-axiom verification; more threads supply no mathematical or novelty evidence.",
    "R99 and R100/R101 are different chunks and R100/R101 ran concurrently; their20.531/26.015/27.953-second measurements are not matched same-chunk j1/j2 or j2/j3 evidence. No speedup estimate is certified."
  ],
  "efficient_future_strategy": [
    "Retain the currently measured2-process/-j2 approach under existing guards, source-locked continuous dispatch and dated bounded checkpoints rather than restarting a full setup for every pair.",
    "Use actual completed timings/guard logs over more chunks to distinguish source complexity, CPU contention, import/receipt overhead and resource waits; no new performance instrumentation or source edits proposed here.",
    "A simple workload planning model for1945 remaining chunks at roughly28seconds each and2 simultaneous jobs gives about7.6hours of compiler wall time before audits/import/receipt/checkpoint variability. This is arithmetic planning only, not a forecast or achieved throughput.",
    "Root directs no j3 candidate or pilot now; such a change would need separate evidence, fresh memory/commit gates, explicit reviewed dispatch and source/axiom-preserving qualification."
  ],
